    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0494" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4722: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-20T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1919,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2355. For the Secretary of State and McCormick:<anchor n="9" xml:id="d403-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Referring my 2343 and 2346 yesterday’s date, Consul General Harris reports Omsk
                    Government is very anxious to learn what the nature of Allied assistance is to
                    be and, in view of another possible winter campaign against Bolsheviki, if such
                    help may be expected soon. In this connection he reports June 18 officially
                    announced Ufa abandoned and now occupied by Bolsheviki. Fighting still in
                    progress around city. I shall be relieved to know measures are under way for
                    prompt and tangible support.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d403-f1" n="9" xml:id="d403-f1-content">
                <p>Vance C. McCormick, chairman of the War Trade Board and technical adviser to the
                    Commission to Negotiate Peace.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
